<p><strong>Lack of Diversification Benefits:</strong>
"Investors may benefit from greater diversification by exchanging a concent=
rated stock position for fund shares without triggering a taxable event" [P=
age 22 of Morgan_Stanley_-<em>Global_Investment_Office</em>(GIO).pdf]. This=
 implies that concentrated positions lack the risk mitigation that comes fr=
om diversification.</p>
<p><strong>Forfeiture of Voting Rights:</strong>
When holding concentrated single-stock positions, "Investors may forfeit th=
eir stock voting rights" [Page 22 of Morgan_Stanley_-<em>Global_Investment_=
Office</em>(GIO).pdf].</p>
<p><strong>Liquidity Constraints:</strong>
"Investment may be illiquid for several years" [Page 22 of Morgan_Stanley_-=
<em>Global_Investment_Office</em>(GIO).pdf].</p>
<p><strong>Leveraged Risk:</strong>
"Investments may be leveraged or contain derivatives" [Page 22 of Morgan_St=
anley_-<em>Global_Investment_Office</em>(GIO).pdf], which can amplify losse=
s in concentrated positions.</p>
<p><strong>Principal Loss Risk:</strong>
"Investment risk and potential loss of principal" [Page 22 of Morgan_Stanle=
y_-<em>Global_Investment_Office</em>(GIO).pdf].</p>
